            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Weekly High-Frequency Issues</h2>
<p>Based on support requests received by Yiyu Digital Media this week, compliance issues clustered around three main scenarios:</p>
<p><strong>1. Creative Copy Touching Platform Red Lines</strong></p>
<p>Multiple operators reported that ad creatives used absolute terms like "guaranteed results," "100% safe," and "no side effects," triggering Meta's misleading content policies. A utility app targeting the US market had its account flagged for using "clinically proven" language without supporting documentation.</p>
<p><strong>2. Landing Page Mismatches</strong></p>
<p>This was the leading cause of account suspensions this week. Missing privacy policy statements, expired SSL certificates, or discrepancies between product features and descriptions all trigger platform risk controls. A cross-border e-commerce team changed their landing page domain during a promotional season without updating compliance filings, resulting in account suspension after three days of running ads.</p>
<p><strong>3. Payment Link Anomalies</strong></p>
<p>Several cases emerged this week involving account reviews triggered by unusual large充值 amounts or sudden spikes in credit card failure rates. High-value top-ups should be discussed with platform account managers in advance to avoid triggering anti-fraud models.</p>
<h2>Compliance Audit SOP Checklist</h2>
<p>Targeting this week's high-frequency issues, here are actionable inspection steps:</p>
<p><strong>Daily Checks</strong><br />
- Verify ad creative copy for absolute language (guaranteed, never, always)<br />
- Confirm landing page privacy policy links are valid and match target regions<br />
- Review account notification center for pending policy violation alerts</p>
<p><strong>Weekly Checks</strong><br />
- Cross-check landing page content consistency with ad promises<br />
- Test complete user journey from ad click to conversion completion<br />
- Verify alignment between top-up records and account spending</p>
<p><strong>Pre-Campaign Checks</strong><br />
- Submit domain whitelist applications 72 hours in advance<br />
- Prepare compliance documentation for claims in creatives (e.g., efficacy statements)<br />
- Confirm account historical credit standing with agency representatives</p>
<h2>Actionable Recommendations</h2>
<p>If your account is already under review, avoid repeatedly submitting appeals. Complete remediation based on the checklist above first, then submit re-review requests through official support channels. For high-value accounts, consider assigning dedicated compliance personnel or implementing third-party audit tools for real-time monitoring.</p>
<p>Compliance is not a one-time task but an ongoing risk management process. Most issues this week could have been detected through standardized audits. This checklist should help your team minimize losses from unexpected campaign pauses.</p>
